---
description: Reefq guardrails for UI, landing, video and theme work
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root in full. The essentials:

- Visual work only. Never edit `netlify/` (except a new id in `netlify/lib/themes.mts`), `netlify.toml`, `package*.json`, `.env*`, `test/`, `tools/guard.mjs`, `.github/`, `.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `public/assets/{commande,invite,analytics,site-bar,wording-templates,phone}.js`, `public/assets/vendor/`, `public/studio/studio.js`, `public/apercu.html`, `tools/seed.mjs`.
- In `public/assets/engine.js` never change the RSVP/data functions (`esc`, `rng`, `hash`, `pad`, `loc`, `fmtDate`, `namesOf`, `initials`, `waLink`, `mapsHref`, `rsvpHtml`, `wireRsvp`, `renderRsvp`, `envOpts`, `couple`, `pairText`, `hostsOf`, `hostsLines`, `hostsMsg`), the `window.ReefqInvite` keys, or existing theme ids.
- Arabic: `dir="rtl" lang="ar"` on Arabic fields and text, `<bdi>` for Arabic inside French text, never retype Arabic wording in code; check screens in Arabic at 360 px. Groom's name first by default.
- Never rename or remove an element `id`, a class used by JavaScript, a form `name`, or a `data-*` attribute. Add new classes instead.
- Brand: videos have no audio track and no music; no images of women (including AI-generated); no alcohol, dancing or nightlife. Never mention these rules in copy.
- Before finishing: run `npm run guard` and `npm test`. If the guard fails, undo the change it names; never edit the guard or tests to pass.
